  "breaths": [
    {
      "id": "s0-0",
      "sceneId": "s0",
      "text": "*Blessed above all women Shall Jael the wife of Heber the Kenite be.* Jael, a queen in Heaven Surely will speak out straight in defence of me."
    },
    {
      "id": "s0-1",
      "sceneId": "s0",
      "text": "Shall I despair Salvation? Was Sisera then more ripe for the knife or nail Than rat-soul'd Becker? Do I misread the tale?"
    },
    {
      "id": "s0-2",
      "sceneId": "s0",
      "text": "I was no stealthy serpent. (Jael flattered and killed her man as he slept.) I was a lion, I challenged before I leapt."
    },
    {
      "id": "s0-3",
      "sceneId": "s0",
      "text": "Three times I gave clear warning (Fair-play's good sport), then standing I struck him dead. Ram-faced lecher, the blood on his own beast head!"
    },
    {
      "id": "s0-4",
      "sceneId": "s0",
      "text": "*Blessed above all women Shall Jael the wife of Heber the Kenite be.* Ah, she won fame for her triumph, My inward joy was payment enough for me."
    },
    {
      "id": "s1-0",
      "sceneId": "s1",
      "text": "Old Becker crawling in the night From his grave at the stair-foot, Labours up the long flight, Feeble, dribbling, black as soot, Quakes at his own ghostly fright."
    },
    {
      "id": "s1-1",
      "sceneId": "s1",
      "text": "A cat goes past with lantern eyes Shooting splendour through the dark. Murder! Help! a voice cries In nightmare; the son dreams that stark In lead his vanished father lies."
    },
    {
      "id": "s1-2",
      "sceneId": "s1",
      "text": "A stair-top glimmer points the goal. Becker goes wavering up, tongue-tied, Stoops, with eye to keyhole.... There, a tall candle by her side, Delilah sits, serene and whole."
    },
    {
      "id": "s1-3",
      "sceneId": "s1",
      "text": "Her fingers turn the prayer-book leaves, Her forehead hints no mental strife: Soft and calm her breast heaves: *So calmly, with his cobbling knife She stabbed him through* ... now never grieves."
    },
    {
      "id": "s1-4",
      "sceneId": "s1",
      "text": "Baffled, aghast with hate, mouse-poor, He glares and clatters the brass knob ... *Through his heart it slid sure: He bowed, he died with never a sob, Again she stabbed*, now sits secure."
    },
    {
      "id": "s1-5",
      "sceneId": "s1",
      "text": "Praying as she has always prayed For great Victoria's Majesty, Droning prayer for God's aid To succour long dead Royalty, The Consort Prince, Queen Adelaide...."
    },
    {
      "id": "s1-6",
      "sceneId": "s1",
      "text": "She falls asleep, the clocks chime two; Old Becker sinks to unquiet rest. Loud and sad the cats mew: Lead weighs cruelly on his breast: His bones are tufted with mildew."
    },
    {
      "id": "s2-0",
      "sceneId": "s2",
      "text": "What's that, who's that comes breaking on my sleep With groans? What, father, you? (The very look, The same smudged foolish face like an old sheep Even after twenty years scarcely mistook.)"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2-1",
      "sceneId": "s2",
      "text": "Speak, Father, speak; that night what came to you Vanished in wrath or terror? Tell the tale; Your beer left still in mug, your half-made shoe On last, your turnip ticking on its nail!"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2-2",
      "sceneId": "s2",
      "text": "*\"Son, it was Death. I have not stirred a foot Out of this horrible dwelling all these years, But planted like a kail I have taken root* Under the stairs, my son, under the stairs._"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2-3",
      "sceneId": "s2",
      "text": "*\"Do not avenge me, Henry. Let all slide. I grudge your death. See, do not touch the snake. A cowardice taints you from your father's side And a coward's lusts, but curb them, for my sake!*"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2-4",
      "sceneId": "s2",
      "text": "\"Back to your grave, back Father, lest she wake!\""
    },
    {
      "id": "s3-0",
      "sceneId": "s3",
      "text": "Two full hours before the dawn, Dotard Parrot cocks an ear To the sleeper's moan, long-drawn, To her slurring tale of fear."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3-1",
      "sceneId": "s3",
      "text": "Parrot hears Delilah tell Who lies dead below the stair; How he shuddered, stumbled, fell; In whose cause she laid him there."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3-2",
      "sceneId": "s3",
      "text": "*The knife bit, thus: thus, the blood spread!* Connoisseur of fo'c'stle speeches Parrot tilts his bald, sly head, Learns the spicy yarn she teaches."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3-3",
      "sceneId": "s3",
      "text": "Soon, when sunlight warms his cage, He plots to cheer the passers-by With burlesque of murderous rage, Acting how his victims die: Thus, he stabs 'em; there, they lie."
    },
